ions  which have regrouped in uh the  northeastern part near the city of  kramatursk uh you you might remember  this city where a missile had hit a  train station killing 59  civilians and they are also regrouping  uh near several donuts so we are  expecting  more uh strikes more artillery fights in  that region with also last night the  other style steel plant  continues continuously being shared and  russia saying it has  begun storming within the steel plan  which is the last bastion of ukrainian  resistance in the city of mariopol  all right emmanuel thanks for that  update dw's emmanuel shaz speaking to us  from lev  earlier i asked our correspondent fanny  fascia and keeve what these strikes in  the west might signal  well basically russia wants to advance  you just describe it uh they shifted  their focus after this unsuccessful  assault in kiev from february 24th they  shifted it now third months into this  war more and more towards the donbass  region but also to the southern apart of  ukraine however these are not the only  parts of ukraine that experiences heavy  shelling as we heard and seen in that  report also in the viv actually a part  of ukraine western ukraine that so far  was relatively spayed from attacks is  also coming on the more intensified  attack uh lately with the most recent  reported by the living mayor there of uh  water and electricity infrastructure  being hit however if you look at the  donbass region especially when you  listen to the governor's day of the  luhan scandanas region basically there's  hardly any place left there where  civilians can be a safe or feel safe and  in fact the governor of luhansk pointed  out it's not just becoming really  impossible to evacuate people from the  landscape region for example but also  just to remove dead bodies from the  streets so you can imagine of course  that the situation there is very very  desperate for people but not only there  obviously the focus has been also during  the past week